Abstract = {Traditionally, environmental management is the responsibility of
   municipal governments. However, recognizing the multiple causes of
   environmental problems, identify new players involved in the process:
   the community, the government and the university. The community: an
   actor par excellence beneficiary acting as a service seeker
   ``cooperation for sustainable development.{''} The state or government:
   whose mission should guide their actions toward coordinating efforts and
   potential towards common goals and objectives. The university, as an
   alternative source of scientific knowledge whose mission for the
   purposes of this investigation, must direct its substantive functions of
   teaching, research and extension, to the design, implementation and
   evaluation of the processes leading to sustainable development, since
   many areas as academic offerings available and functional. This article
   refers to the model MOP-GECUDES 48-166CIS (by its Spanish acronym). The
   model suggests strategies for the procurement of planned approaches to
   sustainability conditions. These strategies are based on cooperation
   processes applicable within the municipal area, in which act as
   ``cooperation partners{''} university education institutions, agencies
   with responsibility for development and community. The philosophical
   approach raises overall orientation toward academic excellence model as
   a way to promote social change successful. The methodological approach
   suggests strategic planning and integrated approach ``logical
   framework{''} as planning and evaluation tools. As tools for collective
   knowledge building socialized.The operational approach suggests
   standardizing components organization strategies, training, funding, and
   communication and information technology support. Finally, the strategic
   approach raises decentralization, collaborative, participatory,
   transdisciplinary and socializing. The focus of the author proposes that
   the figure of the teacher is restated from the notion of the instructor,
   the facilitator or manager cooperation projects. No impairment of
   instructional actions clearly explicit in its natural role. So taken,
   the project manager, in the classroom, only have to change the
   perception from the traditional figure of the ``student in training to
   proactively pre-professional in early exercise of its powers{''}. This
   article reports the partial results of the study. This is a study of
   socio-educational nature with environmental focus. It is developed
   through the use of tools for collecting, analyzing and processing
   information based on focus groups. The focus groups have been comprised
   of 120 surveyed university authorities in the area of extension, 65
   authorities and government officials and more than 270 community
   representatives. The model consists in a systematic and ongoing process
   that begins in the ``colective diagnosis{''} of a problem as the
   starting point. In a first time, an individual work was performed.
   After, this results were integrated by the colective and
   transdisciplinary approach. In this phase, were identified gaps in
   environmental management systems.This diagnosis or detection of
   individual thought arises and / or collective and in the latter case,
   since collective intra or inter, who from their roles and / or
   competency deficiencies detected in environmental management systems
   that translate into sustainable development challenges. Finally,
   strategies were designed to optimize university cooperation for
   sustainability.},
