Year = {2017},
Volume = {23},
Number = {8},
Pages = {7614-7617},
Month = {AUG},
Note = {2nd International Research Conference on Business and Economics (IRCBE),
   Semarang, INDONESIA, AUG 03-04, 2016},
Abstract = {Metrosexual is a term for those men who live in metropolitan cities and
   are concern about their appearance. In fact, they are willing to spend a
   considerable amount of money and efforts to boost their self-images and
   lifestyles. With the rapidly growing male grooming market, this trend
   presents a huge opportunity for companies to pay more attention in
   understanding whether metrosexual men really care about their facial
   care product. The purpose of this study is to examine the relationship
   and to determine the effect of factors influencing the purchase
   intention of metrosexuals towards men's facial care products.
   Self-administered questionnaires were distributed to 200 metrosexual
   men's in Kuala Lumpur. The variables investigated are price
   consciousness and attitude towards purchase intention of men's facial
   care product. The results indicate that attitude was found to be
   significant with strong correlation and positive relationship with the
   purchase intention scale. Other than that, the relationship between
   price consciousness and attitude of respondents was found to be
   contingent on purchase intention. Based on the findings, implications
   for companies are discussed and further research is suggested.},
