Abstract = {Artificial intelligence (AI) systems do not exhibit human-like common
   sense. The principles and practices of experimental psychology -
   specifically, work on infant cognition - can be used to develop and test
   AIs, providing insight into the building blocks of common sense. Here,
   we describe how the evaluation team for DARPA's Machine Common Sense
   program is applying conceptual content, experimental design techniques,
   and analysis tools used in the field of infant cognitive development to
   the field of AI evaluation.},
