Note = {International Conference on Business, Management, Tourism and
   Hospitality (BIZMATOUR), Malacca, MALAYSIA, MAY 12-14, 2015},
Abstract = {For tourism to become a sustainable development strategy, support from
   the residents is needed. Past research have shown different factors such
   as residents' socio demographic characteristics and their cultural
   structure may influence their dispositions toward tourism, thus
   influencing their support toward tourism development. This paper is
   about establishing a conceptual framework of tourism participation by
   residents in Aceh Province who are characterized by Islamic law and
   culture. To this end, previous research and writings on community
   participation, tourism and religion are reviewed and analyzed. The paper
   concludes with propositions for future studies in exploring Aceh
   resident support for tourism.},
