   THE MAIN STREAM OF THE WEIHE RIVER},
Booktitle = {ENERGY, ENVIRONMENTAL \& SUSTAINABLE ECOSYSTEM DEVELOPMENT},
Year = {2016},
Note = {International Conference on Energy, Environmental \& Sustainable
   Ecosystem Development (EESED), Yunnan, PEOPLES R CHINA, AUG 21-23, 2015},
Abstract = {Streambed vertical hydraulic conductivity (K-v) plays an important role
   in understand the water exchange and contaminant transport system
   between streams and groundwater flows. The tests were conducted at 464
   test points in 10 test sites to measure the vertical hydraulic
   conductivity (Kv) for the streambed by applying the falling-head
   standpipe permeameter. Traditional and geostatistics statistics were
   applied to determine the spatial variability of hydraulic conductivity.
   The K-v test values range in 0.01 similar to 61.32 m/d with an average
   value of 4.62 m/d. The maximum frequency distributions occurred between
   0 similar to 5 m/d. The spatial distribution of the sediment hydraulic
   conductivity indicates that the K-v is the biggest in sites 5 and 6,
   then in sites 7 and 8, followed by sites 1 and 2. The K-v values in the
   sites 3,4,9,10 are similar and relatively small, with values being the
   smallest in sites 9 and 10. Along the direction of flow, the K-v values
   in sites 3 and 4 gradually decrease, and those in sites 5 similar to 10
   gradually increase. The K-v values in sites 1 and 2 firstly increase and
   then decrease.},
