   is to implement novel, adaptive, and sustainable tools for assessing
   land degradation in multi-use landscapes in South Africa. This
   presentation demonstrates results from hyper-temporal Sentinel-1 and -2
   timeseries concerning woody cover mapping in complex savanna systems,
   invasive slangbos bush encroachment in grassland areas and regional soil
   moisture retrievals. Validation has been performed by cross-comparisons,
