Abstract = {The increasing number of reported fires or other catastrophes (see Table
   1) occurring in large events leads to the interesting question of why
   preventive design-related and organizational measures have not been
   taken. It also confirms the need to rethink existing building codes and
   safety concepts, as well as inclusion of new ways to optimize buildings
   and event sites. This research project ``KEINE\_PANIK{''}
   ``NO\_PANIC{''} deals with planning criteria in regards to orientation
   in public buildings (such as airports, train stations, meeting halls or
   areas, concert halls, stadiums, etc.) during high-stress situations and
   its influence on the right choice of evacuation routes. The potentials
   of simulation-data optimizing the safety of persons in buildings must be
   included to the planning process, the same as the results of the
   different research groups should be applied in the three dimensional
   procedure of architectural design.},
